  {
   "date": "1966",
   "kind": "occupancy",
   "description": "FeBe's leather bar opened here in 1966 and made Folsom Street the anchor of the city's leather scene; it displayed a sculpture by artist Mike Caffee recasting Michelangelo's David in motorcycle garb, and by the late 1970s hosted the Mr. SF Leather contest that became the International Mr. Leather competition.",
   "source": "lgbtq-context-statement"
